/**
 * Supplementary and profile (prof.dat) information to named characters.
 *
 * There should be an entry for every character in the game.
 *
 * Required fields:
 *   - profileID: the merc ID; the index in the gMercProfiles array. It must corresponds to the data file names
 *   - internalName: the internal name used for logging or mapping other data
 *   - type: what kind of profile it is (corresponds to the ubWhatkindOfMercAmI). It must be one of:
 *        - "AIM": soldiers hired via A.I.M.
 *        - "MERC": soldiers hired via M.E.R.C.
 *        - "IMP": player-character created on I.M.P.
 *        - "RPC": Recruitable characters - NPCs that can be recruited
 *        - "NPC": Non-playing characters, that can never be controlled by the player
 *        - "NOT_USED": Reserved slots that are not used anywhere
 * The rest are optional. If omitted the corresponding value is taken from the prof.dat file.
 * Array fields (e.g. inventory) fully overwrite the prof.dat values. The rest are merged.
 * For instance, if only the health stat is defined here the other stats will be applied from prof.dat.
 * While if there is an inventory field here all the prof.dat items will be discarded.
 *
 * The entries below are complete: they were generated from the merged prof.dat and
 * JSON data (original English version, 1.12) with the JA2_DUMP_MERC_PROFILES developer
 * tool, so every field is defined here explicitly and prof.dat is not needed for them.
 * The full name and the nickname are language dependent and live in
 * mercs-profile-names-<language>.json (for a language without such a file they are taken
 * from prof.dat). Together with mercs-relations.json this makes prof.dat unnecessary for
 * the English version; it is only read for a language without a names file, or when the
 * environment variable JA2_USE_PROF_DAT is set.
*/
